#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1210 expect=skipped domain=DM
#note "THE RFICDTC ALL-FACET GATE (Fix #331 bucket 2, M2-D24 / M3-D18; pin owed by review S9 and authored by Fix #340). The DM dataset deliberately declares no RFICDTC column, so Requirements.Variables.All [RFICDTC] rejects the dataset and the rule is SKIPPED naming RFICDTC. Remove the All entry and the rule EXECUTES: since Fix #330 retired the injected var_exists guard, a bare empty(RFICDTC) is TRUE on every row of an absent column (absent = all-missing) and nothing else in the Check restricts the rows, so it would fire on EVERY row -- the flood the gate exists for. If this scenario EXECUTES (violation or silent pass), the gate has been removed -- escalate, do not rewrite the pin."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SUBJID   type=Char label="Subject Identifier for the Study"
col RFSTDTC  type=Char label="Subject Reference Start Date/Time"
col RFXSTDTC type=Char label="Date/Time of First Study Treatment"
col RFXENDTC type=Char label="Date/Time of Last Study Treatment"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | 001 | 2020-01-01 | 2020-01-02 | 2020-03-15
S1 | DM | 002 | 002 | 2020-01-05 | 2020-01-06 | 2020-03-01
